WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.600 align:start position:0%
I have a question. What's the biggest
asteroid that ever hit Earth? Turns out

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:10.600 align:start position:0%
the one that hit the dinosaurs wasn't
that big. On the very small scale, you

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:13.500 align:start position:0%
have asteroids that are as tiny as a dog
all the way up to the size of a

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:17.500 align:start position:0%
building, and there are likely millions
of these closer to us than Mars. And

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.800 align:start position:0%
they hit us all the time, but our
atmosphere protects us. But then there

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:24.800 align:start position:0%
are the city killers. These are about
the size of a building to about two city

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:28.500 align:start position:0%
blocks. When one of these hit Earth in
1908, it only glanced off our

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:34.600 align:start position:0%
atmosphere, and it still released the
equivalent of 15 megatons of TNT and

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:38.600 align:start position:0%
flattened 80 million trees. But then one
size up is country killer, and then

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:42.700 align:start position:0%
anything bigger than that they call a
planet killer. It would change all life

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:49.900 align:start position:0%
on Earth forever. The rock that hit the
dinosaurs was roughly 10 km across, but

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:54.400 align:start position:0%
1.8 billion years ago, a nearly 15 km
wide rock slammed into what's now

00:00:51.800 --> 00:01:00.200 align:start position:0%
Canada. And 170 million years before
that, the largest asteroid we have

00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:04.199 align:start position:0%
evidence of hitting Earth, 20 km wide,
struck what is now South Africa. But

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:08.700 align:start position:0%
good news, we found about 99% of the
biggest asteroids near us. But the city

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:12.800 align:start position:0%
and country killers, that's the biggest
hole in Earth's defenses right now. To

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:15.800 align:start position:0%
find out how people are trying to fix
it, subscribe.

